## maxogden/csv-spectrum — CSV parsing acid-test corpus

The conformance tests reproduce the full corpus published at
https://github.com/maxogden/csv-spectrum, pinned at commit
`d30e80f8b99d2eecb3778f1d7b9ed1cb425502ec` (tag `2.0.0`, 2024-07-04):

  * vendored verbatim under `src/testdata/csv-spectrum/` (12 `csvs/*.csv` +
    12 `json/*.json` fixture pairs, matched by basename per the corpus's own
    `index.js`)
  * driven mechanically by `src/csv_spectrum_vectors.zig` (one entry per
    pair, `@embedFile`d) and `src/csv_spectrum_test.zig` (the runner, which
    compares this module's parse of each `.csv` against its paired `.json` —
    never against this module's own prior output)

Excluded from vendoring, deliberately: the repository's own `.git/`,
`readme.md`, `index.js`, `test.js`, `package.json`/`package-lock.json`
metadata (none of it is test-fixture data).

CORRECTED 2026-09-09. This file used to conclude: "the repository carries no
separate `LICENSE` file at the pinned commit … so there is no license TEXT to
reproduce beyond that declaration". That inference is wrong. `BSD-2-Clause` is
an SPDX identifier — it names a specific, published licence text, and declaring
it in `package.json` incorporates that text by reference exactly as committing
a copy would. Clause 1 then asks that the copyright notice, the conditions and
the disclaimer be retained by anyone redistributing the material. Whether
upstream got round to committing a file containing them changes nothing about
what a redistributor owes; it only means the text has to be sourced from the
licence itself. It is reproduced below.

